{# AO · THE IDENTITY FACTS, DEMOTED.

   These used to be four KPI plates at the top of this page, which told an area manager that the
   first question of the morning is how many square kilometres the area has. It is not, and it has
   not changed since the area was gazetted. One quiet band, one line, and the link to where the
   facts are managed — and it is a widget like any other, which is why "Attention queue" is allowed
   to sink it to the foot of the page.

   A FACT THE APP DOES NOT HAVE IS SHOWN AS MISSING, NOT LEFT OUT. Dropping the field silently
   would make the band look complete and quietly shrink the area's identity to whatever happens to
   be filled in; an em dash with one word saying why is what sends somebody to Area settings. #}
{% macro fact(key, value, note) %}
    <span class="f">
        <span class="k">{{ key }}</span>
        <span class="v">{{ value|default('—') }}{% if note %}<em>{{ note }}</em>{% endif %}</span>
    </span>
{% endmacro %}
{% import _self as band %}
<div class="ao-ident">
    {{ band.fact('Area', by.host.areaKm2|number_format, 'km²') }}
    {{ band.fact('Zones', by.host.zoneCount, by.host.zoneCount ? 'presence-driven' : 'none yet') }}
    {# Stations are a field concept the host does not model: no station entity, no coordinates, no
       reporting state. It is named here because the area HAS them — leaving the field out would
       claim the identity of an area is complete without them. #}
    {{ band.fact('Stations', null, 'not recorded') }}
    {{ band.fact('IUCN', by.host.iucn, by.host.iucn ? null : 'not set') }}
    {{ band.fact('Established', by.host.established, by.host.established ? null : 'not set') }}
    {{ band.fact('Centroid', by.host.centroid, by.host.centroid ? null : 'no boundary') }}
    <span class="sp"></span>
    <a class="more" href="{{ urls.settings }}">Area settings →</a>
</div>
